[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) merged <ProblemCount ticket={4471} /> reports about dates into one
ticket and marked it known, with one fix queued. The reports describe three different bugs. The
queued parser fix closes only the first one.

<Callout kind="warn">
Not one issue. Three bugs, three tickets. Fixing the parser leaves the other two open.
</Callout>

## The three problems

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} {tickets} />

1. **`parser`**: <ProblemCount ticket={4471} problem="parser" /> reports. The shared parser reads
   every date month first, and every tenant in #4471 writes the day first. Day and month swap in
   the app, in email and in booking-v2 forms.
2. **`hint`**: <ProblemCount ticket={4471} problem="hint" /> reports. booking-v3 prints
   `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field. People type what the hint says, and the form reads it day
   first. This happens only through the form, only at booking-v3 tenants, and a parser fix does not
   touch it. The 4471 page already shows this row as "no ticket of its own".
3. **`one-day`**: <ProblemCount ticket={4471} problem="one-day" /> reports. The booking lands one
   day early instead of swapping day and month. One invite arrived before the booking was made, and
   one meeting showed as Tuesday in Lisbon and Monday in Toronto. This looks like a time-zone bug.
   The desk noted these reports as a one-day move (`desk-notes.json`), but the 4471 page counts them
   under `parser` by tenant.

## How the count is made

- One id, one report: the export pages overlap, so duplicate rows are dropped first (`uniqueById`).
- A report's problem follows its tenant's locale and booking form (`causes.ts`), not the tag intake
  guessed from the reporter's browser. The two disagree on the reports in the "intake tagged
  otherwise" column.
- Reports in `desk-notes.json` → `oneDayMove` are their own problem, `one-day`.

## Why they were merged

[Decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) treats reports as one issue when their subject
lines match, and nobody reads the body. The same subjects come in for all three bugs: "Date is
wrong" and "Wrong day on the invite" each appear under `parser`, `hint` and `one-day`. The
subject cannot tell the bugs apart. Tenant and channel can, as the [cause check](/kb/triage/dedupe)
shows. Changing the rule needs a new decision record, because 0001 stays as it was accepted.

